# Google Maps JavaScript API key.
# Enable these APIs on the key:
#   - Maps JavaScript API   (the interactive map)
#   - Directions API        (routing from the user's location)
#   - Places API (New)      (optional: ratings/hours/photos on the selected place)
#
# "Places API (New)" is the one to enable, NOT the legacy "Places API" — the app
# uses the Place class (searchByText / fetchFields); PlacesService is Legacy.
#
# Places data is DISPLAY-ONLY here and is deliberately excluded from the PDF/ZIP
# export: the Maps Platform terms forbid exporting Google Maps Content or saving
# business names, addresses and reviews. Exports use OpenStreetMap + Wikimedia,
# which are licensed for redistribution.
#
# Restrict the key by HTTP referrer before deploying — it is exposed to the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# A Map ID is required for Advanced Markers. `DEMO_MAP_ID` works for local
# development; create your own in the Google Cloud console for production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=DEMO_MAP_ID

# Where the Express backend is running.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
